#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:6
msgid "CLI Reference"
msgstr "CLI tilvísun"

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:11
msgid "Synopsis"
msgstr "Yfirlit"

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:23
msgid ""
"If no files are given, ``snapper`` reads from stdin and writes to stdout."
msgstr ""
"Ef engar skrár eru gefnar les ``snapper`` af stdin og skrifar á stdout."

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:28
msgid "Options"
msgstr "Valkostir"

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:33
msgid "``-f``, ``--format <FORMAT>``"
msgstr "``-f``, ``--format <FORMAT>``"

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:35
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Input format. One of: ``org``, ``latex``, ``markdown``, ``rst``, "
"``plaintext``."
msgstr "Inntakssnið. Eitt af: ``org``, ``latex``, ``markdown``, ``plaintext``."

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:38
msgid ""
"Auto-detected from file extension when omitted. Defaults to ``plaintext`` "
"for stdin."
msgstr ""
"Sjálfgreinist frá skráarendingu þegar sleppt er. Sjálfgefið er ``plaintext`` "
"fyrir stdin."

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:44
msgid "``--stdin-filepath <PATH>``"
msgstr "``--stdin-filepath <PATH>``"

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:46
msgid ""
"Assume this filename when reading stdin, for format auto-detection. Useful "
"for editor integrations that pipe buffer contents."
msgstr ""
"Gera ráð fyrir þessu skráarheiti þegar lesið er af stdin, fyrir sjálfvirka "
"sniðgreiningu. Gagnlegt fyrir samþættingu ritla sem pípa innihald biðminnis."

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:49
msgid "Example: ``cat paper.org | snapper --stdin-filepath paper.org``"
msgstr "Dæmi: ``cat paper.org | snapper --stdin-filepath paper.org``"

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:54
msgid "``-o``, ``--output <FILE>``"
msgstr "``-o``, ``--output <FILE>``"

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:56
msgid "Write output to a file instead of stdout."
msgstr "Skrifa úttak í skrá í stað stdout."

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:61
msgid "``-i``, ``--in-place``"
msgstr "``-i``, ``--in-place``"

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:63
msgid "Modify input files in place. Requires file arguments (not stdin)."
msgstr "Breyta inntaksskrám á staðnum. Krefst skráarviðfanga (ekki stdin)."

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:69
msgid "``-w``, ``--max-width <N>``"
msgstr "``-w``, ``--max-width <N>``"

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:71
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Maximum line width. Sentences exceeding this width are wrapped at atomic "
"word boundaries (links, inline code, math, and similar tokens stay on one "
"line). Default: ``0`` (unlimited). Also respects ``max_line_length`` from "
"``.editorconfig`` if present."
msgstr ""
"Hámarkslínubreidd. Setningar sem fara yfir þessa breidd eru umbrotnar við "
"orðamörk með ``textwrap``. Sjálfgefið: ``0`` (ótakmarkað). Virðir einnig "
"``max_line_length`` úr ``.editorconfig`` ef til staðar."

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:79
#, fuzzy
msgid "``--clause-breaks``"
msgstr "``--check``"

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:81
msgid ""
"Prefer soft breaks after independent-clause punctuation (comma, semicolon, "
"colon, em dash, ASCII ``--``). Off by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:84
msgid ""
"With ``--max-width 0`` (the default), insert a newline after every such mark "
"that is already followed by whitespace. A sentence that is already one "
"independent clause stays one line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:87
msgid ""
"With ``--max-width`` set, overflowing sentences prefer those marks; a "
"sentence that already fits stays on one line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:89
msgid ""
"Tokens such as ``1,000``, ``10:30``, URLs, ``--flags``, and unspaced dashes "
"never split. ``--check`` uses the same mode when the flag or "
"``clause_breaks`` config is on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:95
#, fuzzy
msgid "``--format-code``"
msgstr "``--lang <CODE>``"

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:97
msgid ""
"After in-block comment reflow, pipe each code-block body through the "
"``formatter`` argv from ``[code.<lang>]`` in ``.snapperrc.toml`` (if "
"present). Default is off so subprocesses are never spawned unless requested. "
"Missing binaries, non-zero exits, and a ~30s timeout are non-fatal; the "
"reflowed body is kept and a diagnostic may be written to stderr."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:104
msgid "``--check``"
msgstr "``--check``"

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:106
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Check mode for CI. Exits with code 1 if any file would change, without "
"modifying anything. Prints the paths of files that would be reformatted to "
"stderr. With no file arguments, checks stdin (JSON/SARIF on stdout, same "
"exit codes)."
msgstr ""
"Prófunarstilling fyrir CI. Hættir með kóða 1 ef einhver skrá myndi breytast, "
"án þess að breyta neinu. Prentar slóðir skráa sem myndu endursníðast á "
"stderr."

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:114
msgid "``--diff``"
msgstr "``--diff``"

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:116
msgid ""
"Show a unified diff of what would change, without modifying anything. Useful "
"for reviewing before committing. Exits with code 1 if any file would change."
msgstr ""
"Sýna sameinaðan diff af því sem myndi breytast, án þess að breyta neinu. "
"Gagnlegt til rýni áður en lagt er inn. Hættir með kóða 1 ef einhver skrá "
"myndi breytast."

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:123
msgid "``--range <START:END>``"
msgstr "``--range <START:END>``"

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:125
msgid ""
"Only format lines in the given range (1-indexed, inclusive). Lines outside "
"the range pass through unchanged. Useful for editor format-selection "
"integrations."
msgstr ""
"Aðeins sníða línur innan tiltekins bils (1-númerað, meðtalið). Línur utan "
"bilsins fara í gegn óbreyttar. Gagnlegt fyrir samþættingu sniðvals í ritli."

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:129
msgid "Example: ``snapper --range 10:20 paper.org``"
msgstr "Dæmi: ``snapper --range 10:20 paper.org``"

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:134
msgid "``--output-format <text|json|sarif>``"
msgstr "``--output-format <text|json|sarif>``"

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:136
msgid ""
"Output format for ``--check`` mode. Default: ``text`` (prints filenames to "
"stderr)."
msgstr ""
"Úttakssnið fyrir ``--check`` stillingu. Sjálfgefið: ``text`` (prentar "
"skráarnöfn á stderr)."

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:139
msgid ""
"``json`` : outputs a JSON array of files, each with ``would_reformat`` and a "
"``diagnostics`` array of 1-indexed ``line`` / ``kind`` (``fused`` / "
"``wrap`` / ``long``) / ``excerpt``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:141
msgid ""
"``sarif`` : outputs SARIF v2.1.0 for GitHub Code Scanning, with one result "
"per diagnostic (``snapper/fused``, ``snapper/wrap``, ``snapper/long``) plus "
"``snapper/needs-reformat`` when the file would change"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:146
msgid "``--strict-long``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:148
msgid "Treat advisory ``long`` diagnostics as ``--check`` failures."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:150
msgid ""
"A ``long`` finding is never the sole cause of exit 1 unless this flag is "
"set. The threshold is ``--max-width`` when that is non-zero, otherwise "
"``long_threshold`` from ``.snapperrc.toml`` (default 120)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:156
msgid "``--neural``"
msgstr "``--neural``"

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:158
msgid ""
"Use neural sentence detection via nnsplit (byte-level LSTM, tract backend). "
"Downloads and caches the model (~4MB) to ``~/.cache/nnsplit/`` on first use. "
"Rule-based detection remains the default (faster, better abbreviation "
"handling). Neural excels for non-English text."
msgstr ""
"Nota taugakerfisstuðða setningargreiningu gegnum nnsplit (bæta-stigs LSTM, "
"tract-bakendi). Hleður niður og vistar eredlíkanið (~4MB) í ``~/.cache/"
"nnsplit/`` við fyrstu notkun. Reglubundin greining er áfram sjálfgefin "
"(hraðvirkari, betri meðhöndlun skammstafana). Taugakerfisgreining er "
"yfirburða fyrir texta á öðrum tungumálum en ensku."

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:166
msgid "``--lang <CODE>``"
msgstr "``--lang <CODE>``"

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:168
msgid ""
"Language for neural sentence detection. Default: ``en``. Available: ``en``, "
"``de``, ``fr``, ``no``, ``sv``, ``zh``, ``tr``, ``ru``, ``uk``."
msgstr ""
"Tungumál fyrir taugakerfissetningargreiningu. Sjálfgefið: ``en``. Tiltæk: "
"``en``, ``de``, ``fr``, ``no``, ``sv``, ``zh``, ``tr``, ``ru``, ``uk``."

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:175
msgid "``--model-path <PATH>``"
msgstr "``--model-path <PATH>``"

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:177
msgid ""
"Path to a custom ONNX model file for neural detection. Overrides ``--lang``."
msgstr ""
"Slóð að sérsniðinni ONNX eredlíkansskrá fyrir taugakerfisgreiningu. "
"Yfirgegnir ``--lang``."

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:183
msgid "``--use-pandoc``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:185
msgid ""
"Require the pandoc path (auto FFI, then CLI). Parse may use in-process FFI "
"when ``libsnapper_pandoc`` loads; the writer still needs ``pandoc`` on "
"``PATH`` (``libsnapper_pandoc`` is reader-only) unless that library exports "
"a writer. Without FFI, both parse and write use the ``pandoc`` CLI. A "
"missing binary is an explicit error (never silent all-prose). Enables "
"support for typst, asciidoc, docx, html, and all other pandoc-supported "
"formats. The default (omit this flag) already uses pandoc when an FFI writer "
"or ``pandoc`` on ``PATH`` is available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:195
msgid "``--native``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:197
msgid ""
"Force today's native line parsers (markdown / org / rst / latex / "
"plaintext). Conflicts with ``--use-pandoc``. Use this when you want source-"
"oriented splice instead of the pandoc writer. Editors, wasm, and LSP stay "
"native even without this flag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:205
msgid "``--pandoc-backend <auto|ffi|cli>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:207
msgid ""
"How to obtain the pandoc AST when the pandoc path is used. ``auto`` "
"(default) prefers in-process FFI, else CLI. ``ffi`` requires "
"``libsnapper_pandoc`` (explicit error if missing). ``cli`` uses a ``pandoc`` "
"subprocess (explicit error if missing). The writer still needs ``pandoc`` on "
"``PATH`` when the FFI library has no writer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:216
msgid "``--config <PATH>``"
msgstr "``--config <PATH>``"

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:218
msgid ""
"Path to a ``.snapperrc.toml`` config file. When omitted, ``snapper`` "
"searches from the current directory upward."
msgstr ""
"Slóð að ``.snapperrc.toml`` stillingarskrá. Þegar sleppt er leitar "
"``snapper`` frá núverandi möppu og upp á við."

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:224
msgid "``-h``, ``--help``"
msgstr "``-h``, ``--help``"

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:226
msgid "Print help message."
msgstr "Prenta hjálparskilaboð."

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:231
msgid "``-V``, ``--version``"
msgstr "``-V``, ``--version``"

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:233
msgid "Print version."
msgstr "Prenta útgáfunúmer."

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:238
msgid "Subcommands"
msgstr "Undirskipanir"

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:243
msgid "``snapper init``"
msgstr "``snapper init``"

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:245
msgid ""
"Initialize snapper for a project. Detects which prose formats exist in the "
"directory tree and generates:"
msgstr ""
"Frumstilla snapper fyrir verkefni. Greinir hvaða textasnið eru til staðar í "
"möpputrénu og býr til:"

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:248
msgid "``.snapperrc.toml`` with sensible defaults"
msgstr "``.snapperrc.toml`` með skynsamlegum sjálfgildum"

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:250
msgid "``.gitattributes`` entries for the git smudge/clean filter"
msgstr "``.gitattributes`` færslur fyrir git smudge/clean síuna"

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:252
msgid "pre-commit hook snippet"
msgstr "pre-commit hook bútur"

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:254
msgid "Apheleia (Emacs) configuration snippet"
msgstr "Apheleia (Emacs) stillingabútur"

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:256
msgid "Use ``--dry-run`` to preview without writing files."
msgstr "Notaðu ``--dry-run`` til að forskoða án þess að skrifa skrár."

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:261
#, fuzzy
msgid "``snapper sdiff <OLD> <NEW>``"
msgstr "``snapper init``"

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:263
msgid ""
"Sentence-level diff between two files. Parses both files, extracts "
"sentences, diffs at sentence granularity. Whitespace reflow produces zero "
"diff. Colored output by default; use ``--no-color`` to disable. Exits with "
"code 1 if differences found."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:272
msgid "``snapper git-diff [REF] [FILE...]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:274
msgid ""
"Sentence-level diff against a git ref. Default ref: ``HEAD``. If no files "
"specified, diffs all changed prose files (``.org``, ``.tex``, ``.md``). Uses "
"``git show REF:path`` to retrieve the old version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:282
msgid "``snapper watch <PATTERNS...>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:284
msgid ""
"Watch files and auto-reformat on save. Accepts file paths or glob patterns. "
"200ms debounce to avoid reformatting during rapid saves. Press Ctrl+C to "
"stop."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:291
#, fuzzy
msgid "``snapper lsp``"
msgstr "``snapper init``"

#: ../../source/reference/cli.rst:293
msgid ""
"Start the Language Server Protocol server on stdin/stdout. Provides document "
"formatting, range formatting, and diagnostics (flags lines with multiple "
"sentences). Works with any LSP-compatible editor (Neovim, Emacs eglot, VS "
"Code, Helix)."
msgstr ""

